    <body>
      <div type="clause" n="32.1">
        <head><ref type="lawCode" target="law:VIAtr">VI Atr</ref> 32.1</head>
        <ab type="liebermannText" xml:lang="ang" source="#liebermann" n="32.1" corresp="#wit-d-incomplete">and swa ymbe feos bote, þ<hi rend="italic">æt</hi> an mynet gange ofer ealle þas þeode buton ælcon false.</ab>
        <ab type="editionText" xml:lang="ang" source="#robertson" n="32.1" corresp="#wit-k">⁊ swa ymbe feos bote þæt an mynet gange ofer ealle þas þeode butan ælcon false.</ab>
        <ab type="editionText" xml:lang="ang" source="#rabin-doml" corresp="#wit-k">And swa ymbe feos bote, þæt an mynet gange ofer ealle þas þeode butan ælcon false.</ab>
        <ab type="translation" xml:lang="en" source="#robertson" corresp="#wit-k">And the coinage shall be improved by having one currency, free from all adulteration, throughout all the country.</ab>
        <ab type="translation" xml:lang="en" source="#rabin-doml" corresp="#wit-k">The currency is to be improved so that there is one standard coinage throughout the realm without any adulteration.</ab>
        <ab type="translation" xml:lang="de" source="#liebermann">und so auf Münzreform, dass Eine Münze über all dies Land hin gehe ohne jedes Falsch.</ab>
        <ab type="translation" xml:lang="en" source="#claude" ana="#fromGerman">and on reform of the coinage, so that one coinage may be current throughout all this nation without any falseness.</ab>
        <note type="editorial">Liebermann compares III Eg 8.</note>
      </div>
